✗ Cross-arch check FAILED.

  One or more crates do not compile for aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.

  WHY THIS CHECK EXISTS:
  Every other blocking lane builds target_arch = "x86_64", so an item
  referenced ONLY from inside a cfg(target_arch = "x86_64") block looks
  used everywhere it is checked — and is dead code on ARM64, which CI
  builds with -D warnings.  #1037 proved this: simd_activations.rs left
  SIMD_MIN_LEN, vector_path_available and 26 MLAS polynomial constants
  reachable only from x86_64 code, breaking both ARM64 lanes at the
  compile step while every x86_64 job stayed green.

  FIX: gate x86-only items with cfg(target_arch = ...) alongside their
  only consumer, or — when portable tests still need them — mark them
  #[cfg_attr(not(target_arch = "x86_64"), allow(dead_code))].
